$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Small nonstationary SWAN example on a regular grid
$ Three spatially uniform wind fields are interpolated over one hour
$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------

PROJECT 'NSTREG' '001'
SET NAUTICAL
MODE NONSTATIONARY TWODIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

$ Computational grid: 20 x 10 meshes; compact spectral discretization.
CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 2000.0 1000.0 20 10 &
      CIRCLE 24 0.05 1.0 32

$ Constant 20 m depth on a 2 x 2 input grid.
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 1 1 2000.0 1000.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 3 0 FREE

$ Time-dependent Cartesian x/y wind input at 00:00, 00:30 and 01:00.
$ SWAN updates the forcing at the one-minute computational time steps.
INPGRID WIND REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 1 1 2000.0 1000.0 &
        NONSTATIONARY 20260101.000000 30 MIN 20260101.010000
READINP WIND 1.0 'wind.wnd' 3 0 1 0 FREE

$ Constant waves enter from the west; the initial field is explicit.
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 1.0 6.0 270.0 20.0
INITIAL PAR 0.5 5.0 270.0 25.0

GEN3 KOMEN
BREAKING CONSTANT 1.0 0.73
FRICTION JONSWAP CONSTANT 0.038

$ Write seven time levels, including both ends of the one-hour window.
BLOCK 'COMPGRID' NOHEADER 'nonstationary_regular_hs.blk' LAYOUT 3 HSIGN &
      OUTPUT 20260101.000000 10 MIN
POINTS 'CENTER' 1000.0 500.0
TABLE 'CENTER' HEADER 'nonstationary_regular_center.tbl' &
      TIME TSEC XP YP WIND HSIGN TM01 DIR &
      OUTPUT 20260101.000000 10 MIN

COMPUTE NONSTATIONARY 20260101.000000 1 MIN 20260101.010000
STOP
